'''Loras''' is an [[NPC]] located in the {{Zone|Tangleburg Library}}. They tell the player lore about the [[Precursor (disambiguation)|Precursors]] and [[Starborn (disambiguation)|Starborns]].

== Dialogue ==
{| class="wikitable"
!Condition
!Dialogue
|-
| class="ct" | None
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Greetings, traveler.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: I'm Loras, a historian dedicated to uncovering the secrets of the &5Precursors&f.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Sadly, their history is shrouded in mystery, with scarce records surviving.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: I've had to piece together their story through fieldwork and ancient relics.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: My dream? To pen a comprehensive tome about them, but the pieces are still falling into place.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Interested in what I've uncovered so far?<br>&eSelect an option: &a[Yes] &c[Later, maybe]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&c[Later, maybe]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Understandable. History has a way of capturing us when we least expect it.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Feel free to return if curiosity strikes.}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[Yes]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Ah, a fellow history enthusiast! Excellent.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Through my research, I've deducted that the Precursors were this world's first inhabitants.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Remarkably, they lived under the watch of multiple entities called &9Starborns&f!<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: I've identified at least eight Starborns, but I suspect there were more.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Each Starborn had a unique domain and wielded immense power.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[What kind of domain?]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[What kind of domain?]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: From the Starborn of the Forests or the Sea, even a Starborn of Life!<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: It's unclear whether the Precursors were creations of these Starborns, but they certainly revered them.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: My studies led me to distinguish two categories: Old and New Starborns.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[Not very original.]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[Not very original.]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Ah, but the names reflect a theory.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: The Old Starborns seemen indifferent to mortal affairs, transcending earthly desires.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Conversely, the New Starborns engaged actively with the Precursors, reveling in their advancements and guiding their progress.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: I believe that immortals who maintain worldly interests and desire could be considered 'young' in a divine sense.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[It's an interesting theory]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[It's an interesting theory]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Much appreciated.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: The New Starborns were particularly invested, almost as proud mentors observing their wards' milestones.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: They even intervened directly at times, teaching essential lessons like substainable living and the imporance of nature's balance.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[So the Starborns were spectating them]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[So the Starborns were spectating them]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Precisely, but also guiding. <br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: For instance, they introduced magic to the Precursors, a decision with unforeseen consequences.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: The Precursors ended up excelling in both magic and science, eventually blending the two to create wonders.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[I see where this is going]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[I see where this is going]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Their ambition grew boundless.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: They sought more: longer life, greater strength, boundless energy.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Later generations of Precursors, born into a world of accomplishments, yearned for purpose and legacy.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: For those young generations of Precursors, it became impossible to define their own purpose in the shadow of monumental achievements.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Something had to happen, the wheel of progress had to keep turning.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: So one day, a bold claim arose: the Precursors had surpassed the Starborns.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: They saw the Starborns' teachings as shackles, hindering their true potential.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[Those Precursors are very human after all]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[Those Precursors are very human after all]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Indeed... But this hubris marked the beginning of the end.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: The Precursors harnessed their tools and magic to overpower the Starborns.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Adding to this, the Starborns' power was intrinsically tied to the belief of their followers.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: As the Precursors' faith diminished, so too did the might of the Starborns, weakening them in this crucial confrontation.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[Can Starborns even die?]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[Can Starborns even die?]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: That remains a mystery. But it's clear that their influence faded.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: As for the Precursors, they vanished without a trace, a puzzling paradox.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[So how does the story end?]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[So how does the story end?]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Here's my theory: aware of their impending doom, the Starborn of Time, perhaps the most powerful due to universal belief, made a desperate move.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: He propelled the Precursors far into the future, hoping that by then, others could stand against them.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[The future? When exactly?]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[The future? When exactly?]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: That's the unknown.<br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: But it suggests that the Precursors might reemerge one day, a thought both fascinating and daunting.<br>&eSelect an option: &a[So the Precursors will just appear out of nowhere one day?]}}
|-
| class="ct" | Selecting {{Rmt|&a[So the Precursors will just appear out of nowhere one day?]}}
|{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: It's a possibility we cannot ignore. <br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: We must be prepared for whatever comes. <br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Thank you for lending an ear to my life's work. <br>&e[NPC] &bLoras&f: Now, I must return to my studies.}}
|}

